<%- include('../partials/layout-start') %>

<%- include('../partials/page-header', {
  icon: 'bi-people',
  heading: 'Refer someone',
  sub: 'Bring someone in, and earn when they actually pay for something.'
}) %>

<section class="glass-section pb-5">
<div class="container">
  <%- include('../partials/flash') %>

  <div class="row g-4">
    <div class="col-lg-7">
      <div class="glass-card">
        <div class="card-body">
          <h2 class="h5">How it works, in full</h2>
          <ul class="mb-4">
            <li>You get a link. Anyone who creates an account through it is attributed to you.</li>
            <li>
              <strong>You earn <%= rateBps / 100 %>%</strong> of what they pay, capped at
              <%= maxCommission %> per payment, and only on things that pay commission:
              <%= commissionableProducts.join(' and ').replace(/_/g, ' ') %>.
            </li>
            <li>
              Commission is credited when the money is <strong>actually received</strong> — not when a
              quote is produced, not when a checkout is opened.
            </li>
            <li>
              Attribution lasts <strong><%= windowDays %> days</strong> for earning. The record of who
              introduced whom is permanent; the earning window is not, so nobody carries an open-ended
              claim on someone else's future.
            </li>
            <li>You are paid once your balance reaches <%= minPayout %>. Below that it keeps accruing — it is never lost.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="h6">Things worth knowing before you join</h2>
          <ul class="small text-muted-2 mb-4">
            <li>You cannot refer yourself. The check is in the attribution, not in the terms.</li>
            <li>
              First touch wins, permanently. If someone was already attributed to another member,
              a later link does not move them — a scheme whose attribution can be taken has a fight in it.
            </li>
            <li>
              Your dashboard shows how many people you introduced and what each earned. It does not
              show who they are: they did not agree to have their purchases reported to you.
            </li>
            <li>
              Payouts are made by a person, by bank transfer or PayPal, against the details you give us.
              Nothing is transferred automatically.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <form method="post" action="/referrals/join">
            <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
            <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Get my link</button>
          </form>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="col-lg-5">
      <div class="glass-card">
        <div class="card-body">
          <span class="icon-tile icon-amber mb-3"><i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle"></i></span>
          <h2 class="h6">Be realistic about the amounts</h2>
          <p class="small text-muted-2 mb-0">
            Most of what this Hub does is free, and it intends to stay that way. There are two paid
            things, so a referral earns when someone features a job or pays a project deposit — and
            not otherwise. That is a real but modest amount of money, and we would rather say so
            here than have you work it out from an empty balance.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</section>

<%- include('../partials/layout-end') %>
